==German==

===Etymology===
Perhaps from {{m|de|Amt|Amts-}} + ''simile'' (from {{etyl|la|de}} {{m|la|simile||similar}}), the name of a standardized form used by the bureaucracy of the Austria Empire. Alternatively, perhaps a reference to the service horses ({{m|de|Amt|Amts-|official}} + {{m|de|Schimmel||white horse}}) which were provided in Switzerland and elsewhere to government officials.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Amtsschimmels|-}}

# excessive amount of bureaucracy; [[red tape]]

====Derived terms====
* {{m|de|der Amtsschimmel wiehert||there is an excessive amount of bureaucracy}}
